                <note rend="inline" type="source">824.6363 ST 2/202: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Bolivia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Caldwell</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-12-06T16:00:00-05:00">December 6, 1937—4
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>32. Your telegrams 70, December 3, 2 p.m., and 71, December 3, 3 p.m. The
                    Department is of the opinion that, until you are informed of the definite
                    decision by the Junta, you should take no further action in the case except to
                    follow and report upon important developments. Air mail instruction follows.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
